[{:db/id 17592186124448 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b2a9101c-1b4a-5430-a447-8fae79ba4cdb" "question-e1ce51ab-65e5-5a2f-a7f1-d19c74e60108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124254 :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $f_x(x,y)=x+2y$ and $f_y(x,y)=2y-x$\n\nII. $f_x(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$ and $f_y(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$\n\nIII. $f_x(x,y)=-\\sin{x}\\sin{y}$ and $f_y(x,y)=\\cos{x}\\cos{y}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124449 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17f2fd35-823f-52a1-8bc6-17fa0dd0fd8c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2a9101c-1b4a-5430-a447-8fae79ba4cdb" :question/id #uuid "b2a9101c-1b4a-5430-a447-8fae79ba4cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-133235" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(x,y)=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+a{y}^{2},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=bx\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+6xy.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+a{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-2yx\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2ay \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(bx\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+6xy) \\\\  & =b\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-bxy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-2yx\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2ay & =b\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-bxy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+6y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $y$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ respectively, we see that $a=3$ and $b=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a912a37-363a-53e6-bf86-dbe48185fc08"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a912a37-363a-53e6-bf86-dbe48185fc08" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a912a37-363a-53e6-bf86-dbe48185fc08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-467fecb4-2ef9-52a6-963f-3519ca79e412" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e269130c-3006-5fed-9abb-a6de955d0350" "answer-8dc86f81-73d2-56a8-b320-2c1bc2c18f7a" "answer-40357cb7-ceb7-5912-9a08-22064ac23e43" "answer-467fecb4-2ef9-52a6-963f-3519ca79e412" "answer-4a53e719-2052-591b-812c-8d7bafb6fb97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e269130c-3006-5fed-9abb-a6de955d0350" :answer/id #uuid "e269130c-3006-5fed-9abb-a6de955d0350" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dc86f81-73d2-56a8-b320-2c1bc2c18f7a" :answer/id #uuid "8dc86f81-73d2-56a8-b320-2c1bc2c18f7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40357cb7-ceb7-5912-9a08-22064ac23e43" :answer/id #uuid "40357cb7-ceb7-5912-9a08-22064ac23e43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-467fecb4-2ef9-52a6-963f-3519ca79e412" :answer/id #uuid "467fecb4-2ef9-52a6-963f-3519ca79e412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a53e719-2052-591b-812c-8d7bafb6fb97" :answer/id #uuid "4a53e719-2052-591b-812c-8d7bafb6fb97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=8,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e1ce51ab-65e5-5a2f-a7f1-d19c74e60108" :question/id #uuid "e1ce51ab-65e5-5a2f-a7f1-d19c74e60108" :question/math-academy-id "q-133224" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{3}y+10xy, \\\\ {f}_{x}(2,1) & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3) \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y-0 \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{3}y+10xy) \\\\  & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a{x}^{2}y+10y & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${x}^{2}y,$ we get $b=\\frac{2}{3}a.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{x}(2,1)=14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,1) & =14 \\\\ a(2)^{2}(1)^{2}+5(1)^{2}-3 & =14 \\\\ 4a+2 & =14 \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $b=\\frac{2}{3}a=\\frac{2}{3}(3)=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-843bf297-f481-59fb-a7e7-1153b03b247c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-843bf297-f481-59fb-a7e7-1153b03b247c" :answer-field/id #uuid "843bf297-f481-59fb-a7e7-1153b03b247c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-17ff528c-3c19-55ef-aada-a825dbe38568" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2e70829-198b-5fba-9007-e3b43ddb0346" "answer-1a612995-7d65-55d6-92a3-415ca7d3151e" "answer-17ff528c-3c19-55ef-aada-a825dbe38568" "answer-090cb572-cfdb-5f1c-ab62-85230fae9ba1" "answer-6d620e7d-0d60-5dad-a3b6-8c6c1da4471c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2e70829-198b-5fba-9007-e3b43ddb0346" :answer/id #uuid "b2e70829-198b-5fba-9007-e3b43ddb0346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a612995-7d65-55d6-92a3-415ca7d3151e" :answer/id #uuid "1a612995-7d65-55d6-92a3-415ca7d3151e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17ff528c-3c19-55ef-aada-a825dbe38568" :answer/id #uuid "17ff528c-3c19-55ef-aada-a825dbe38568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-090cb572-cfdb-5f1c-ab62-85230fae9ba1" :answer/id #uuid "090cb572-cfdb-5f1c-ab62-85230fae9ba1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d620e7d-0d60-5dad-a3b6-8c6c1da4471c" :answer/id #uuid "6d620e7d-0d60-5dad-a3b6-8c6c1da4471c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=\\frac{2}{3},\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186383342 :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268926 :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{e}^{3x+2y}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{e}^{3x+2y}+6xy$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=4{y}^{2}-15{x}^{2}y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=8xy-5{x}^{3}$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6x{y}^{3}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-17f2fd35-823f-52a1-8bc6-17fa0dd0fd8c" :question/id #uuid "17f2fd35-823f-52a1-8bc6-17fa0dd0fd8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-133394" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(4,1,7)$ given that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n{f}_{xz}(x,y,z)=2x\\sqrt{z-3y}+z{e}^{x-4y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{xzy}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xz}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\sqrt{z-3y}+z{e}^{x-4y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{z-3y}})-4z{e}^{x-4y} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{z-3y}}-4z{e}^{x-4y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point  $(4,1,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(4,1,7) & =-\\frac{3\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{7-3\\cdot 1}}-4\\cdot 7\\cdot {e}^{4-4\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{7-3}}-28{e}^{4-4} \\\\  & =-6-28 \\\\  & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61f81261-3e5b-587f-b2ff-a3f22db029b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61f81261-3e5b-587f-b2ff-a3f22db029b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "61f81261-3e5b-587f-b2ff-a3f22db029b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b450a0c-622f-59cc-b892-e0e3a7245713" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f497807-e3fd-59ce-901a-13ca8829f6a8" "answer-ed3fd222-7c6c-5f15-a429-78af9dfec4a2" "answer-3b450a0c-622f-59cc-b892-e0e3a7245713" "answer-9507cee6-c36c-51c1-88e0-630f702efac1" "answer-b3d39e69-ac71-52bc-b3fa-32d9dee16b58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f497807-e3fd-59ce-901a-13ca8829f6a8" :answer/id #uuid "5f497807-e3fd-59ce-901a-13ca8829f6a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed3fd222-7c6c-5f15-a429-78af9dfec4a2" :answer/id #uuid "ed3fd222-7c6c-5f15-a429-78af9dfec4a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b450a0c-622f-59cc-b892-e0e3a7245713" :answer/id #uuid "3b450a0c-622f-59cc-b892-e0e3a7245713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9507cee6-c36c-51c1-88e0-630f702efac1" :answer/id #uuid "9507cee6-c36c-51c1-88e0-630f702efac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3d39e69-ac71-52bc-b3fa-32d9dee16b58" :answer/id #uuid "b3d39e69-ac71-52bc-b3fa-32d9dee16b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125729 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $f(x,y) = x y^2 - x^3 y.$ Then the first-order partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} (x,y) = y^2 -3x^2y \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x,y) = 2xy -x^3,\n$$\n\nand the second-order **mixed partial derivatives** are \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}(x,y) = 2y -3x^2 \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad  \\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}(x,y) = 2y-3x^2.\n$$\n\nNotice that these two mixed partial derivatives are equal, i.e., \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}=\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}.\n$$\n\nIn general, if a function $f(x,y)$ has continuous first-order partial derivatives on an open set $U,$ and the second-order mixed partial derivatives exist and are continuous on $U,$ then the mixed partial derivatives are equal everywhere on $U.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124742 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
